 just in our fast-paced lives we  don't get to do  that signature combo boxing and yoga  speaks volumes yes  in the beginning of class i'm taking you  up getting the heart rate up you give  all the effort  that you can want you to feel as strong  as you possibly can  and then you're sweaty and then i get  you to connect to your heart  people bring their palms together and i  would say certain affirmations that if  it doesn't challenge you it doesn't  change you  like your love your kindness and  compassion all come from your heart  but your courage your bravery your  strength all come from the same place  all right i want the energy up you  wouldn't have that mindset without the  yoga you'd be all in fight mode  this allows you to take out that  aggression and then bring that  level of calmness inhale in  and release without it where would you  be without  finding a practice i don't know where i  would be i would probably be depressed i  would probably  may have been one of the people to snap  or go off i wouldn't  be in a place where i'm at peace and and  enjoy this 34 year old believes it can  help in  healing and training officers who  protect and serve  double time one twos i want the best for  police officers  i truly feel that the training is  setting officers up for my experience  to not win i truly believe that some  type of  martial arts discipline practice and  yoga practice  consistently throughout your entire  career can help a person  just regulate their emotions for police  officers or police officers  for anyone i think that being trained  gives you a certain confidence that you  don't need to go grabbing for your gun  and and that's the key you know i first  heard martisa's story about two years  ago when  i took one of his classes uh and when i  when i saw what happened to george floyd  i  immediately i immediately thought of him  and remember that dave chappelle  um 848 46 stand up that he did  he talked about how police officers who  had seen bad  things done and then reported them what  happened to them some of them being  fired from the force and how they took  it internally and and snapped as a  result that's what he was describing he  says  i don't want my fellow officers my  former fellow officers  to have to go through this it would be  so wonderful if they found what i  found and so that's why i thought it was  important to tell us yeah and i love  that he also  says for anyone not just for police but  certainly you can see that i mean you've  taken yoga i know  yeah and actually i wish that class was  here in new york because boxing and yoga  combined you're right the woman in the  piece that said you get that aggression  out  and then you center yourself let's do it  all right

